file, You can obtain one at http://mozilla.org/MPL/2.0/.

Scope, because this directory also holds someone else's work
-------------------------------------------------------------

This file covers the snake mark only:

    w-w3.svg, w-w3-16.png, w-w3-22.png, w-w3-24.png, w-w3-32.png,
    w-w3-48.png, w-w3-64.png, w-w3-128.png, w-w3-256.png

It does NOT cover anything under gnupg/, which is GnuPG's own artwork
and carries its own terms -- GPL version 3 or later, or CC-BY-SA 4.0
for the logos, and SIL Open Font License 1.1 for the three banner
fonts. See gnupg/README (verbatim, from upstream) and gnupg/PROVENANCE.md
for which licence applies to what. Do not read this file as relicensing
anything under gnupg/.

No trademark rights are granted here. The MPL grants copyright
permission, not permission to use a name or a mark, and this fork's mark
is deliberately not derived from either party's artwork -- see design
section 11.9.2.

Where the drawing came from
---------------------------

Drawn procedurally for this fork: a centreline curve expanded into a
filled polygon with a width profile, shaded by concentric shells, with
the head as part of the same tube. No part of it is traced from, or
recoloured from, Mozilla's bird or GnuPG's wing.

One element has a documented outside origin and it is not in these
files: the message indicator that accompanies this work embeds the wing
from GnuPG's artwork, under GnuPG's licence. That graphic lives with
design section 14, not here.
